  "worked_solution": "To graph the function $y=2f(x),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and stretch it by factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $2.$\n\nThe resulting graph is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218586/assets/a88c2321811017dcedf2c83178b47dcf8f314926e1fb2ef4273681def639f2a0.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
